  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ankit Agrawal vs State Of Punjab on 12 July, 2024 Author: Kirti Singh Bench: Kirti Singh Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:090903 Crm-M-14012-2024 (O&M) 1 In The High Court Of Punjab & Haryana At Chandigarh Crm-M-14012-2024 (O&M) Reserved on : 12.07.2024 Pronounced on: 19.07.2024 Ankit Agrawal ..... Petitioner Versus State Of Punjab .... Respondent Coram: Hon'Ble Ms. Justice Kirti Singh Mr. Vinay Kumar, Dag, Punjab.",
    "facts": "Ankit Agrawal vs State Of Punjab on 12 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/89814337/ 1 1 of 5 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:090903 Subsequently, 50 boxes each containing 10x6x10 strips totalling 30,000 tablets of Alprazolam were recovered from the possession of the petitioner from his premise i.e. a medical shop in Shikohabad, Firozabad, Uttar Pradesh.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for the petitioner inter alia submits that the petitioner was arrested from the premises of the medical store in Uttar Pradesh of which he is an authorized signatory since 23.04.2021. He further submits that medical store namely M/s Agrawal Medical Store is the duly licensed seller and distributor of the Alprazolam drug which was seized by the Investigating Agency. The license has been issued by the Food and Safety Drug Administration, an authority under the Government of Uttar Pradesh, under Form 20-B and Form 21-B to the aforesaid firm, which is valid till 31.12.2027. The learned counsel for the petitioner has placed reliance upon the judgments rendered in the cases of \"Tofan Singh Vs State of Tamil Nadu\" (2021) 4 SCC 1, \"Surinder Kumar Khanna Vs Intelligence Officer 2 of 5 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:090903 Directorate of Revenue Intelligence\" (2018) 8 SCC 721, \" Sanjeev Chandra Agarwal & Anr Vs Union of India\" (2021) 20 SCC 57, wherein, the Hon'ble Supreme Court has laid down certain observations regarding release of accused on bail. He also relied upon the judgments passed by this Court in \"Anil Kumar Vs State of Punjab\" (CRM-M-32408-2020), Ajaypal Singh alias Ajay Vs State of Punjab\" (CRM-M-30519-2018), \"Vipul Goyal Vs State of Haryana\" (CRM-M-9492-2021) and \"Harjit Singh Vs State of Punjab\" (CRM-M-37650-2021). As per custody certificate, the petitioner has undergone an actual custody of 06 months and 27 days and there is no other criminal case pending against him. However, the learned State counsel has opposed the bail by submitting that in view of the serious allegations against the petitioner, he is not entitled to the concession of regular bail."
  },
